# Copy to .env.local. Everything is optional for local development.

# --- Database ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Unset → embedded Postgres in .data/pglite with demo data (local only).
# Production: a Postgres URL (Supabase: use the pooler URL; Neon: pooled URL),
# then run `npm run db:migrate` and `npm run create-admin -- ...`.
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://user:pass@host:6543/postgres

# --- Auth ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Required in production. Generate with: openssl rand -base64 32
# AUTH_SECRET=

# --- Geocoding ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Set to use Google Geocoding (more accurate for unit/shop addresses, billed per request).
# Unset → OpenStreetMap Nominatim (free, max 1 request/second).
# GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=
# GEOCODE_COUNTRY=au
# Nominatim asks for a contact in the User-Agent:
# GEOCODE_USER_AGENT=your-company-delivery-planner (ops@example.com)

# --- Road routing -------------------------------------------------------------
# Unset → public OSRM demo server (fine for trials, not for production volume).
# For production, self-host OSRM (Docker) with an Australia extract and set:
# OSRM_URL=http://your-osrm:5000

# --- Google Maps display (recommended) ----------------------------------------
# Set a browser key with "Maps JavaScript API" enabled (restrict it by HTTP referrer
# to your domain). All maps then use Google Maps, with satellite and Street View.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=
# Optional: your own Map ID (Google Cloud → Map Management) for custom styling.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAP_ID=
# Note: GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY above is the *server* key for geocoding (restrict by IP).
# Google's terms require Google geocoding results to be shown on a Google map, so
# use both keys together.

# --- Map tiles (only used when no Google key is set) ----------------------------
# Default is openstreetmap.org tiles (light use only). For production, use a tile
# provider such as MapTiler/Stadia/Thunderforest:
# NEXT_PUBLIC_TILE_URL=https://api.maptiler.com/maps/streets-v2/{z}/{x}/{y}.png?key=YOUR_KEY
# NEXT_PUBLIC_TILE_ATTRIBUTION=&copy; MapTiler &copy; OpenStreetMap contributors

# --- Scheduled order feeds ------------------------------------------------------
# Vercel Cron calls /api/cron/sync-orders with this secret (see vercel.json).
# CRON_SECRET=
